+
+## Capture and optional dependency
+
+macOS capture does not call the deprecated display/window-list screenshot route. It resolves one ScreenCaptureKit shareable window by both observed window ID and owning PID, creates a desktop-independent window filter, bounds the requested image size, encodes PNG with AppKit and returns bytes plus the observed identity fingerprint. `MacOSDesktopAdapter.capture` refuses an unreadable OS version or release older than 12.3 before permission/API access; it then requires non-prompt Screen Recording permission. It lazily imports `ScreenCaptureKit` and reports a typed unavailable result if the optional wrapper is not installed.
+
+The live Desktop extra still omits `pyobjc-framework-ScreenCaptureKit`; its official 12.2.2 PyPI metadata requires `pyobjc-core>=12.2.2`, `pyobjc-framework-CoreMedia>=12.2.2` and `pyobjc-framework-Cocoa>=12.2.2`. The selected CPython 3.12 universal2 wheels and exact URL/SHA/size fields are recorded in the plan-only successor `docs/full_project_continuation_v2/evidence/release_data_lifecycle/desktop-builder-candidate-r3-w25/`. It preserves the two added wheel artifacts (41,019 bytes unique) and rebinds the candidate to the final capture/profile source. `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock` and project version remain unchanged. No package file was downloaded, installed or built.
+
+## Evidence limits
